  "description": "PUTWUX crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C46 H98 Co6 N12 O50 Y4 2+,2(N1 O3 1-),6(C1 H4 O1),7(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Y1 (Y) has 8 O neighbors; Y2 (Y) has 9 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Y1A (Y) has 8 O neighbors; Y2A (Y) has 9 O neighbors; Co1A (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co2A (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co3A (Co) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately linear metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.036-4.023 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.62-114.42°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [CoII2CoIII4YIII4(Htris)8(OAc)6(NO3)4(MeOH)2](NO3)2·6MeOH·7H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies Co(II), Co(III), Y(III).",
